          "create_time": 1792676985.938,
          "update_time": 1792676997.815,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The connection yields a **bounded signed remainder**, while the tested bulk-mass estimate remains weaker than direct critical-value estimation. Saved the derivation in [Note 06](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-4/notes/06_CRITICAL_WALL_TRACES_AND_SIGNED_ENDPOINT_BUDGET_20261022.md).\n\nOn the conditional ordinary-double window, I proved\n\\[\nq=\\frac1t+r,\\qquad |r|\\le K,\\qquad\n\\left|C_2-\\frac{C_0}{t}\\right|\\le K_0t,\n\\]\nwith explicit constants from the existing jet bounds. Consequently,\n\\[\n\\sigma\\!\\left[C_2-\\left(\\frac1t+K\\right)C_0\\right]\\le0.\n\\]\nThis pays the signed amplitude remainder while retaining the compulsory unit logarithmic coefficient.\n\nThe sharp spatial trace is\n\\[\nq^2\\le\\frac{1+P^2}{\\pi r^2}\\int_{|z-c(t)|<r}g_2\\,dA.\n\\]\nI also paid the additional complex-time trace and regulator costs. The resulting specified mass certificate cannot beat the direct bound.\n\nFor the endpoint square trace, subtracting \\(t^{-2}\\) alone is insufficient: it also retains \\(2r_0/t\\), where\n\\[\nr_0=\\frac{C_2C_4+S_3^2}{2C_2^2}.\n\\]\nIts actual theta-source sign remains unpaid. Exact algebra checks and internal review passed; the overview and progress records are updated."
